window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-c302e8415c7f61ad"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"codex-cloud\">Codex Cloud</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"run-coding-tasks-in-the-cloud\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">在云端运行编程任务</h2> <p>你可以让 Codex 在云端处理编程任务，从调查 Bug 到构建功能都可以。之后可在网页、移动应用或桌面应用中检查更改并继续工作。</p> <blockquote> <p>配图：已发布的云端环境旁边显示新任务编辑器，并选中了同一环境</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-here\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">从这里开始</h3> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad?anchor=getting-started\">开始使用</a></li> </ul> <p><a id=\"why-use-codex-cloud\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-cloud_1\">为什么使用 Codex Cloud</h3> <ul> <li><strong>从项目开始：</strong> 选择代码仓库。Codex 会检查项目、执行环境准备步骤，并在缺少信息或访问权限时向你询问。</li> <li><strong>让工作持续进行：</strong> 从已发布的环境启动任务。每项任务都有独立工作区；即使电脑处于睡眠状态，任务仍可继续运行。</li> <li><strong>检查工作成果：</strong> 查看已更改的文件并检查结果；你可以提出后续修改请求，并在准备好后提交更改或创建拉取请求。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"getting-started\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">开始使用</h2> <p><strong>开始使用 Codex Cloud。</strong></p> <p>创建包含项目所需代码仓库、工具和访问权限的云端环境，或选择已有环境，然后启动任务。</p> <p><a id=\"1-open-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"1-chatgpt\">1. 打开 ChatGPT</h3> <p>在网页、移动应用或<a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">桌面应用</a>中打开 ChatGPT，然后登录你的 ChatGPT 账户。</p> <p><a id=\"2-create-or-select-an-environment\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"2\">2. 创建或选择环境</h3> <p>在网页或桌面应用中，选择 <strong>Work in</strong> &gt; <strong>Cloud</strong>，然后打开 <strong>Select environment</strong>。移动设备上请打开 Codex。选择现有环境即可开始工作。若要新建环境，请在网页或桌面应用中选择<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=create-and-publish-an-environment\">创建环境</a>，然后继续下文步骤。</p> <p><a id=\"3-let-codex-prepare-your-project\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"3-codex\">3. 让 Codex 准备项目</h3> <p>选择 GitHub 代码仓库，然后选择 <strong>Get started</strong>。如果系统提示，请连接 GitHub。Codex 会检查代码仓库、安装依赖和工具，并测试工作流程。遇到缺少的访问权限或信息时，请按提示提供。</p> <p><a id=\"4-review-and-publish\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"4\">4. 检查并发布</h3> <p>如果是新环境，请检查设置和测试结果，保存更改并选择 <strong>Publish</strong>。等待状态显示 <strong>Environment published</strong>。</p> <p><a id=\"5-start-a-task\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"5\">5. 启动任务</h3> <p>发布新环境后，选择 <strong>Start a new task</strong>。如果使用的是已有环境，则可以立即开始。描述任务并发送，然后检查更改和测试结果、提出后续修改请求，并在准备就绪后提交更改或创建拉取请求。</p> <p><a id=\"next-steps\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">后续步骤</h3> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">配置云端环境</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">配置互联网访问</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=configure-environment-variables-and-network-secrets\">了解环境变量和网络密钥</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=reuse-and-update-saved-state\">了解如何复用已保存状态</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-345f9e63361a6444\">在 Slack 中使用 ChatGPT</a></li> </ul> <p><a id=\"see-what-codex-cloud-can-do\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-cloud_2\">了解 Codex Cloud 的能力</h2> <p>使用项目工具和服务访问权限运行编程任务，然后检查结果。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=create-and-publish-an-environment\">准备开发工作流程</a>：让 Codex 检查代码仓库，并准备依赖和工具。发布前先查看检查结果。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=reuse-and-update-saved-state\">复用项目设置</a>：在不同任务间复用代码仓库、依赖和工具。每项任务都有自己的工作区；随着项目变化，及时更新设置。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">连接工具和服务</a>：让 Codex 访问项目所需的软件包注册表、API 和私有服务。请配置网络访问，并在环境设置中提供凭据。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"use-codex-cloud-when\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-cloud_3\">适合在以下情况下使用 Codex Cloud……</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">工作需要在远程环境中运行</a>：为 Codex 提供所需的代码仓库和工具。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">多个任务需要相同的环境设置</a>：从已发布的环境启动任务，同时让每项任务的工作状态彼此独立。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">工作流程需要服务凭据</a>：为获准的 HTTPS 服务使用网络密钥，并限制环境可访问的网络目标。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?sectionMissing=cli-codex-cloud\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">从 CLI 启动云端任务（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>：从终端启动任务、查看最近的云端对话并检查其状态。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"codex-cloud\">Codex Cloud</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"run-coding-tasks-in-the-cloud\">Run coding tasks in the cloud</h2> <p>Give Codex coding tasks to work through in the cloud, from investigating bugs to building features. Review changes and continue from the web, mobile, or desktop app.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: A published cloud environment beside a new task composer with the same environment selected</p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"start-here\">Start here</h3> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad?anchor=getting-started\">Get started</a></li> </ul> <h3 id=\"why-use-codex-cloud\">Why use Codex Cloud</h3> <ul> <li><strong>Start with your project:</strong> Choose repositories. Codex inspects the project, works through setup, and asks you for missing details or access.</li> <li><strong>Keep work moving:</strong> Start tasks from a published environment. Each task has its own workspace and can keep working while your computer is asleep.</li> <li><strong>Review the work:</strong> Inspect changed files and check results, request follow-up changes, and commit or open a pull request when you're ready.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"getting-started\">Getting started</h2> <p><strong>Get started with Codex Cloud.</strong></p> <p>Create a cloud environment with the repositories, tools, and access your project needs, or select an existing one. Then start a task.</p> <h3 id=\"1-open-chatgpt\">1. Open ChatGPT</h3> <p>Open ChatGPT on the web, mobile, or in the <a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">desktop app</a>, then sign in with your ChatGPT account.</p> <h3 id=\"2-create-or-select-an-environment\">2. Create or select an environment</h3> <p>On the web or in the desktop app, choose Work in &gt; Cloud and open Select environment. On mobile, open Codex. Select an existing environment to begin working. To create a new one, use the web or desktop app and select <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=create-and-publish-an-environment\">Create environment</a> and continue below.</p> <h3 id=\"3-let-codex-prepare-your-project\">3. Let Codex prepare your project</h3> <p>Choose your GitHub repositories and select Get started. Connect GitHub if prompted. Codex inspects your repositories, installs dependencies and tools, and tests the workflow. Provide any missing access or information when asked.</p> <h3 id=\"4-review-and-publish\">4. Review and publish</h3> <p>For a new environment, review the setup and test results, save changes, and select Publish. Wait for Environment published.</p> <h3 id=\"5-start-a-task\">5. Start a task</h3> <p>After publishing a new environment, select Start a new task. If you selected an existing environment, you can start right away. Describe your task and send it. Review the changes and test results, request follow-ups, and commit or open a pull request when ready.</p> <h3 id=\"next-steps\">Next steps</h3> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">Configure cloud environments</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">Configure internet access</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=configure-environment-variables-and-network-secrets\">Set up environment variables and network secrets</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=reuse-and-update-saved-state\">Understand saved state</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-345f9e63361a6444\">Use ChatGPT in Slack</a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"see-what-codex-cloud-can-do\">See what Codex Cloud can do</h2> <p>Run coding tasks with your project tools and service access, then review the results.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=create-and-publish-an-environment\">Prepare your development workflow</a>: Let Codex inspect your repositories and prepare their dependencies and tools. Review the checks before publishing.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=reuse-and-update-saved-state\">Reuse your project setup</a>: Reuse your repositories, dependencies, and tools across tasks. Each task has its own workspace. Update the setup as your project changes.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">Connect your tools and services</a>: Give Codex access to the package registries, APIs, and private services your project needs. Configure network access and supply credentials in the environment settings.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"use-codex-cloud-when\">Use Codex Cloud when…</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">Work should run remotely</a>: Give Codex a cloud environment with the repositories and tools it needs.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">Several tasks need the same setup</a>: Start tasks from a published environment while keeping each task's working state separate.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">Your workflow needs service credentials</a>: Use network secrets for allowed HTTPS services and limit the environment's network destinations.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?sectionMissing=cli-codex-cloud\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">Start cloud work from the CLI (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">Local page (section not recognized)</a>: Start a task from your terminal, or list recent cloud chats and check their status.</li> </ul>"};
